(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The C API's natives the class :capi-port still named after py-capi-1122 (the burst of 2026-11-25, py-capi-1125;"] [4 1 "// doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: py-capi-1125\"), each written after CPython 3.14.10's function of the same"] [5 1 "// name: PyErr_Display, PyErr_DisplayException, PyErr_Print and PyErr_PrintEx (Python/pythonrun.c), PyCode_Addr2Line"] [6 1 "// (Objects/codeobject.c) and Py_UniversalNewlineFgets (Objects/fileobject.c). The PSF's license (LICENSE.md)."] [17 1 "// cThreads are the C threads PyThread_start_new_thread made, by their Python thread's ident (each a Python thread"] [18 1 "// of _thread's, so the GIL serializes them with the others)."] [21 1 "// cLocks are PyThread_allocate_lock's locks (Python/thread_pthread.h): each a _thread.lock of pyi's (blocking with"] [22 1 "// the GIL released, as PyThread_acquire_lock runs under Py_BEGIN_ALLOW_THREADS in CPython), by the address of the"] [23 1 "// 8 bytes of the world that is the PyThread_type_lock C holds."] [26 1 "// cThreadStack is a C thread's stack (as musl's default for pthread_create: 128 KiB is musl's, the world's C code is"] [27 1 "// CPython's test modules', so 1 MiB)."] [30 1 "// startCThread is PyThread_start_new_thread(func, arg): a Python thread of _thread's whose body runs the C function"] [31 1 "// func(arg) on a C thread of its own (a stack mapped in the world, the main thread's thread-local objects), the"] [32 1 "// mirrors synchronized around it as around a call into C; a fault in it ends the process (World.guard). Its ident,"] [33 1 "// or -1 when the thread cannot start."] [71 1 "// lockOf is the _thread.lock of a PyThread_type_lock (a fault for one PyThread_allocate_lock did not give, as a freed"] [72 1 "// pthread lock's use is undefined)."] [81 1 "// thread is the C thread of the running Python thread: the one PyThread_start_new_thread made for it (capi_rest.go,"] [82 1 "// py-capi-1125), else the world's main thread (the library's). The GIL's holder is the only goroutine that runs C,"] [83 1 "// so each Python thread's C frames stay on a stack of its own."] [93 1 "// displayException is _PyErr_Display(file, NULL, value, tb): a traceback given beside an exception that has none"] [94 1 "// put on it (issue #18776), then traceback._print_exception_bltin(value), which writes sys.stderr (colorized when"] [95 1 "// _colorize says so); when that cannot run, sys.__excepthook__'s own printing."] [110 2 "// the fallback: the built-in hook's printing of the same exception"] [123 1 "// writeStderr is PySys_WriteStderr of a text: sys.stderr.write(s), its errors ignored."] [130 1 "// handleSystemExit is _Py_HandleSystemExit and Py_Exit for an exception that is a SystemExit: its code (None 0, an int"] [131 1 "// its value, anything else printed to sys.stderr and 1), the exit functions run (atexit's, Py_FinalizeEx's first step)"] [132 1 "// and the standard streams flushed, then the process exits. false (nothing done) for any other exception."] [171 1 "// printEx is _PyErr_PrintEx: the raised exception (none: nothing) handed to sys.excepthook(type, value, traceback),"] [172 1 "// sys.last_exc, last_type, last_value and last_traceback set first when setSysLastVars, the audit event"] [173 1 "// \"sys.excepthook\" raised before the call; a hook that fails has its error and the original displayed, a missing hook"] [174 1 "// \"sys.excepthook is missing\" and the exception displayed. A SystemExit exits the process (handle_system_exit)."] [237 1 "// lineOfOffset is PyCode_Addr2Line's _PyCode_CheckLineNumber over code.co_lines(): the line of the range holding the"] [238 1 "// byte offset addr (-1 for a range of no line, or an offset no range holds)."] [268 1 "// fgetsByte is the stream's next byte as getc gives it (-1 at the end or on an error), read by the world's fread into"] [269 1 "// one byte of the world's memory."] [282 1 "// ungetByte is musl's ungetc of a byte just read by fread: the read position stepped back over the buffer's byte"] [283 1 "// (rpos at offset 8 of musl's FILE, never below its buffer after a read of it) and the end-of-file flag (F_EOF, 16)"] [284 1 "// cleared. EOF is not pushed back."] [302 2 "// PyErr_Display(unused, value, tb) and PyErr_DisplayException(exc) (Python/pythonrun.c): the exception printed to"] [303 2 "// sys.stderr as the interpreter prints an uncaught one (traceback's _print_exception_bltin)"] [316 2 "// PyErr_Print() is PyErr_PrintEx(1); the error indicator cleared"] [325 2 "// PyCode_Addr2Line(code, addrq) (Objects/codeobject.c): co_firstlineno for a negative offset, else the line of the"] [326 2 "// address range that holds it (code.co_lines(), the location table's view)"] [350 2 "// Py_UniversalNewlineFgets(buf, n, stream, fobj) (Objects/fileobject.c, _Py_UniversalNewlineFgetsWithSize): at most"] [351 2 "// n-1 bytes of the line, \\r and \\r\\n read as \\n, NUL-terminated; NULL when nothing was read; fobj must be NULL"] [352 2 "// (errno ENXIO otherwise)"] [358 21 "// ENXIO"] [387 2 "// the thread module's natives (Python/thread.c, thread_pthread.h)"] [409 2 "// PyThread_acquire_lock(lock, waitflag): 1 (PY_LOCK_ACQUIRED) or 0; PyThread_acquire_lock_timed(lock, microseconds,"] [410 2 "// intr_flag): microseconds < 0 waits as long as it takes, 0 does not wait"] [440 3 "// a lock not held stays released (thread_pthread.h's semaphore lock posts; the error is no one's to see)"] [444 2 "// PySlice_Unpack (queue 262's, capi_limited.go) when an index of the slice is no int or None: its __index__ is Python"] [445 2 "// code that may change any object C sees (gh-72054: test_slice's PopIndex pops from the list whose Py_SIZE the"] [446 2 "// macro PySlice_GetIndicesEx reads after the call), so the mirrors are synchronized around it as around a call"] [447 2 "// into C: C's writes taken first, then Go's state written back to C"] [463 1 "// plainIndex is a slice index whose evaluation runs no Python code: None or an exact 